{title: Line of Cain}
{subtitle: Genesis 4:18; 4:17–22; 4:19–22}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Dm/F] | [Eb] | [Gm] [Dm/F] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]Cain knew his wife and gave birth to Enoch
[Eb]He built a city and [F]named it his [Bb]son
From [Cm7]Enoch came Irad in the [Gm]dust
Irad was the [Eb]father of [F]Mehu[Gm]jael
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Mehu[Eb]jael was the fa[F]ther of Methus[Gm]hael
Methus[Eb]hael was the fa[F]ther of La[Bb]mech
The line of [Eb]Cain stood a[F]part in the [Gm]world
A lineage [Eb]moving through [F]the ancient [Gm]earth [Eb][F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]Lamech took two wives for himself
[Eb]Adah was the first [F]and Zillah the [Bb]other
[Cm7]Adah gave birth to Jabal the el[Gm]der
Father of tents [Eb][F]and those who keep live[Gm]stock
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]Jubal was the brother of Jabal
[Eb]Father of all [F]who play the lyre and [Bb]pipe
[Cm]Zillah gave birth to Tu-bal-[Gm]Cain
He [Eb]forged tools [F]out of bronze and i[Gm]ron
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Tu-bal-Cain's [F]sister was [Gm]named Naamah
The [Eb]civiliza[F]tion grew in their [Gm]hands
[Eb]Far from [F]the godly line [Gm]of Seth
Their [Eb]names are written in the [F]book of Genesis [Gm]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Irad the fa[F]ther of Mehu[Gm]jael
Mehu[Eb]jael the fa[F]ther of Methus[Gm]hael
The de[Eb]scendants [F]of Cain re[Gm]main [Eb][F][Gm]
{end_of_verse}
